[{:db/id "q-87602/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" :answer/id #uuid "78670e2e-7235-5ef5-845f-79109873fef1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87602/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "5a8c5bfe-15ff-5811-ae3a-3e820997b44e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87602/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "7a6be738-b844-5f4d-8143-ebadfcd158c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87602/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer/id #uuid "423a278e-75f6-536e-829a-6499ae94821b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87602/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02" :answer/id #uuid "3391be23-5ca4-5ad2-8dd9-b8d7ead4c541" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87602/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "22c16416-3348-538c-8e12-b62a20c14703" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87602/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" :answer-field/choices ["q-87602/selection/a84d639d380e10cb74c92005685f9f65779377dfb51342c280c63c645679bbea" "q-87602/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-87602/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-87602/selection/801bcdd9cb6a10cec998162e05f71050c8aaf0c6974f095bdcaef715a09f4aee" "q-87602/selection/59cabed12271767d3647412725d382bc72464274dc4ac46b4e7903c969156a02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87602" :question/id #uuid "3217a78a-1242-5401-848b-e78c5cdbda0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-87602" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $8$ data points, where \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=-56,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=560.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=8$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}=-56,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot (-56) \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2}=560,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 560 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =70-{(-7)}^{2} \\\\  & =70-49 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-87602/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87602"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-87606/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "bc0809c5-ef01-52ec-9b63-b937460e151a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87606/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "cefbdeae-a511-5ab3-af93-fd6e9aa96eaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87606/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "537ecd56-e26b-5a11-939d-eb537acb9c07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87606/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "9e90554b-1261-526c-83cb-8e8439aede5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87606/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "80d28857-1af1-59a2-ae0d-418f6c05c6a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-87606/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ce7a91f-7cad-5def-b2a5-200f3d55d4c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-87606/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-87606/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-87606/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-87606/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-87606/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-87606/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-87606" :question/id #uuid "879601af-b2da-5f0b-bbc6-5fce10bb3cf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-87606" :question/is-example false :question/problem "What is the variance of the following data set?\n\n$$\n1,\\,5,\\,1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,6,\\,1,\\,2,\\,6\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=9$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (1+5+1+2+3+6+1+2+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 27 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot ({1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (1+25+1+4+9+36+1+4+36) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 117 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =13-{(3)}^{2} \\\\  & =13-9 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87606/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0040fc1-2134-5eaa-a3e8-6c7a457f75f5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87606"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263340/field-1/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer/id #uuid "afe6aa64-af78-5b7a-a7e7-4ac14701ea04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263340/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9803225-96c4-5426-a1c0-d3e70f19eb16" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263340/field-1/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer-field/choices ["q-263340/field-1/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263340" :question/id #uuid "82b35b09-23fa-53fe-8257-c05a78815445" :question/math-academy-id "q-263340" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Compute the variance ${\\sigma }^{2}$ of a data set ${x}_{i}$ consisting of $12$ data points, where\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}=-180,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}^{2}=3564.\n$$\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=12$ points in our data set, and we know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}=-180,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot (-180) \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ We know that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}^{2}=3564,$ so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot 3564 \\\\  & =297.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =297-{(-15)}^{2} \\\\  & =297-225 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-263340/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eab4249-544e-56c6-81c0-e6db84033701"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263340"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263585/field-1/266e8548256f6eb1cfd874f9531fe3a017029e86b6267ee0c553a122dd28dce3" :answer/id #uuid "a336db98-e2dc-568a-be6c-cc284ba8b3a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8\\sqrt{41}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263585/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "3c15ddad-12e2-50b5-a3d4-99afc6713ffe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263585/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "93cf3cb4-f063-579d-b843-5746e3f2559c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263585/field-1/266e8548256f6eb1cfd874f9531fe3a017029e86b6267ee0c553a122dd28dce3" :answer-field/choices ["q-263585/field-1/266e8548256f6eb1cfd874f9531fe3a017029e86b6267ee0c553a122dd28dce3" "q-263585/field-1/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263585" :question/id #uuid "3465a7ef-ecfc-5da2-88a3-b3ddd7544d34" :question/math-academy-id "q-263585" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Compute the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n15,\\,1,\\,-10,\\,-13,\\,-9\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=5$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (15+1-10-13-9) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-16) \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot [{15}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-10)^{2}+(-13)^{2}+(-9)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot [225+1+100+169+81] \\\\  & =\\frac{576}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{576}{5}-{(-\\frac{16}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{576}{5}-\\frac{256}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{2880-256}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{2624}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2624}{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{41}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-263585/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a72dae6-2bbf-5e59-b71d-8ee57f589753"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263596/field-1/f94affd71f8d18aaa07c02d32dd09fcf0cb48fca6d4f0e3f430d00cfcbee3f24" :answer/id #uuid "b8d7c561-ebba-5683-8dd2-3e16336f2ff4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{357}}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263596/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "817592ad-1532-5690-8cb1-8201f69d28d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263596/field-1/f94affd71f8d18aaa07c02d32dd09fcf0cb48fca6d4f0e3f430d00cfcbee3f24" :answer-field/choices ["q-263596/field-1/f94affd71f8d18aaa07c02d32dd09fcf0cb48fca6d4f0e3f430d00cfcbee3f24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263596" :question/id #uuid "9f2f806f-af5f-57af-8c6f-9650c646c6b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-263596" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Compute the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n-9,\\,-5,\\,3,\\,8,\\,-1,\\,-4,\\,-6\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (-9-5+3+8-1-4-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (-14) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [(-9)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{8}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-6)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [81+25+9+64+1+16+36] \\\\  & =\\frac{232}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{232}{7}-{(-2)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{232}{7}-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{232-28}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{204}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{204}{7}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{51}{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-263596/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a72dae6-2bbf-5e59-b71d-8ee57f589753"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263596"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
